## 1. Standards documents and corpus — NOT covered, and not redistributable by us

The governing documents live in `pgs_docs/` and are ingested into `knowledge/corpus/`.
They are third-party works. None of them is licensed to us for redistribution.

| Work | Rights position (checked 2026-11-03) |
|---|---|
| `saoso-version-2.1-2026.pdf` | No copyright, reproduction or licence notice anywhere in the text. Absence of a notice grants no permission: default copyright applies. |
| `Outeniqua pgs principles, policies and procedures 2026.pdf` | Same — no rights notice found. |
| `PGS Certification landscape_Final.pdf` | Explicitly: may be copied and adapted for "not-for-profit and/or educational purposes only… cannot be used for commercial purposes"; the logos of SAOSO, KCOA, BMZ and GIZ "must not appear on any adaptation". Copyright PGS South Africa / SAOSO, 2021. |
| `Basic Production Principles_ENG_PRINT.pdf`, `6. … assessment form … .xlsx`, `5. … preparation list.pdf`, `7.a–7.c` | No notice checked. Treat as unknown and therefore not redistributable. |

**Consequence, and why it is deliberate:** the engine ships; the corpus does not. An
operator ingests their own copy of the standard they are certified against. That is also
what makes the engine retargetable to a second standard or a second producer group without
a migration — the architectural rule in `AGENTS.md`.

If you are redistributing this software, do not add those documents to your copy.

